---
import Callout from "../atoms/Callout.astro";
import Accordion from "../atoms/Accordion.tsx";
---

<section
  class="mx-auto mt-1 max-w-md p-4 sm:mt-4 sm:grid sm:max-w-360 sm:grid-cols-7 sm:gap-x-8 lg:px-15 lg:py-6"
>
  <Callout class="sm:col-span-5 sm:col-start-2">
    Watch a 2-minute video to learn<br />about your peers’ experiences
  </Callout>

  <div class="mt-5 sm:col-span-5 sm:col-start-2 sm:mt-6">
    <iframe
      src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/TqV3NN6Aiq8"
      title="YouTube video player"
      allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
      referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
      allowfullscreen
      class="aspect-video h-full w-full"></iframe>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4 sm:col-span-5 sm:col-start-2 sm:mt-6">
    <Accordion
      openingTitle="Read the transcript"
      closingTitle="Hide the transcript"
      client:load
    >
      <div
        class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-pretty sm:col-span-4 sm:mt-px lg:mt-2 lg:space-y-6 lg:text-2xl"
      >
        <p>
          <strong>Daur, University of Oxford</strong> I am a medical oncologist and DPhil
          student working on tumor avatars and translational cancer research. I finished
          the course in one week and honestly, it changed my perspective. and let
          biotech become unveiled for you as well. Good luck!
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Zohar, University College London</strong> I'm a PhD student at UCL
          studying molecular epidemiology and I really resonated with the mission
          of trying to make sure that we can incentivize innovation in the health
          space while also ensuring that everybody has access to medicines. It doesn't
          take that long, so go sign up.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Yushi, University of Oxford</strong> I'm doing a PhD in molecular
          and cellular biology at the University of Oxford. This course connects science
          and the business of drug development with the realities of the US healthcare
          system, particularly insurance reimbursement and how treatments are usually
          paid for, which I wasn't really aware of in the past.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Celine, Imperial College London</strong> I'm currently working at a healthcare
          and life sciences consulting firm in London. I came across the Biotech Unveiled
          through one of Peter Kolchinsky's posts, where he introduces the course
          as a gateway to an extensive fellowship program run directly by Peter himself
          and the No Patient Left Behind team. I recommend this to anyone who is curious
          or interested in the biotech industry in general.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Weronika, University of Southampton</strong> Hi, I'm Weronika and I'm
          currently doing my PhD in cancer research. It really breaks down how drugs
          can actually reach patients. So from development and investment to policy,
          drug pricing, and insurance. It's really insightful, easy to follow, and really
          changes how you think about impact.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Accordion>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  @reference '../../styles/global.css';

  p {
    @apply text-pretty;
    line-height: 138%;
  }

  strong {
    @apply block font-semibold;
  }
</style>
